    description: ""  # cfea
    fields:  # cfea
      severity: "high"  # cfea
      statement: "node.stable_id is documented as 'hypergumbo-stableid-v4' (sha256:<16hex> prefix). In bm.json: 33518 of 33694 (99.5%) use the sha256: prefix form; 176 nodes use one of 5 alternative formats — raw 64-char hex without prefix (156, mostly python methods/functions like 'e324857529d1...'), 'lang:scheme:name:kind' 1-colon form (103, e.g. 'typescript:npm:lit:npm_package'), bare name with 0 colons (25, e.g. 'activate' from service-worker.js), 2-colons (6), 3-colons (2). The mass of 156 raw-hex python entries strongly suggests an early-emission path that skips the prefix wrapper."  # cfea
      root_cause: "Multiple analyzer code paths produce stable_id without going through the canonical-prefix helper. Python method/function analyzer emits raw 64-char hex directly (156 cases). Pass-17 BBBBBB found 60% collision rate; this finding adds the FORMAT-dispersion axis (5+ formats coexist in the same field)."  # cfea
